\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Environment-conditioned query procedure. A semantic target selects configuration-retaining goal candidates; cached capsules provide a conservative broad phase, Dijkstra searches the enabled roadmap, and interpolated MoveIt/FCL checks accept the path or reject one edge and trigger replanning. Rejections are scoped to the current environment revision.}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:query_pipeline}{{1}{3}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Method-specific node construction in a two-dimensional analogue of normalized configuration space, produced by the same deterministic GNG and digit-permuted Halton implementations the system deploys. Marker counts are scaled; labels give the deployed 800-node composition. Pure GNG quantizes the 4,000-sample validity-filtered candidate stream, guarded GNG reserves 599 globally supportive low-discrepancy samples, and Halton/PRM samples directly. Because the goal test is a workspace one, its configuration-space preimage is disjoint, so both inverse-kinematic branches of a single target are drawn. All methods subsequently use the same validated $k$-nearest-neighbor connector.}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:roadmap_construction}{{2}{3}}
